<% content_for :title, "About" %>

<header class="page-header">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>A stock sheet for a small kitchen</h1>
  <p class="lead">Pantry replaces the clipboard on the walk-in door.</p>
</header>

<div class="prose">
  <p>
    Every item has a par level: the amount the kitchen wants on hand at the start
    of service. At close, the cook on shift counts the dry store, walk-in, freezer
    and line, and Pantry flags anything that has fallen below par.
  </p>

  <h2>Two roles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cooks</strong> count stock, add items and keep kitchen notes up to date.</li>
    <li><strong>Managers</strong> do everything cooks do, and also see purchase orders and what they cost.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How counts become orders</h2>
  <p>
    Items below par roll up by supplier. A manager turns that list into a draft order,
    places it, and marks it received when the delivery is checked in.
  </p>
</div>
